## Honesty Covenant (binding — verbatim)

```
1 No red-as-green  2 No scope narrowing  3 No skip-and-assume  4 No stubs as final
5 No parity shortcuts  6 No delegation  7 No predecessor bypass  8 No commit on red
9 No silent drift  10 Log ends with EXIT=<int> and STATUS=<DONE|BLOCKED>
```

Delegation: NONE (implemented directly; no sub-agents used).

## Architecture mapping (web → native)

- useBatteryHealthAnalytics   → BatteryHealthClientFeed (Operations.Analytics.BatteryHealth,
                                GET /analytics/battery-health?vehicle_id=) — primary read; drives the
                                page loading/error/empty state (BatteryHealthAnalytics.FromJson null gate).
- useBatteryDegradation       → BatteryHealthClientFeed (Operations.Analytics.BatteryDegradation,
                                GET /analytics/battery-degradation?vehicle_id=) — best-effort read; only the
                                prediction (with projection_points) is consumed for the capacity-trend chart.
- useChargingSessionsPaginated→ BatteryHealthClientFeed (Operations.Charging.Sessions, GET /charging?
                                vehicle_id=&limit=100&offset=0) — best-effort; powers the charge-level
                                distribution, charging habits, AC/DC breakdown and the smart insights.
- useChargingTelemetryLatest  → BatteryHealthClientFeed (Operations.Charging.TelemetryLatest,
                                GET /charging-telemetry/latest?vehicle_id=) — best-effort; powers thermal
                                monitoring + the Full-Charge-Complete card.
- useSelectedVehicle          → vehicleId passed to the feed (the shell owns the global picker, matching
                                every sibling W7 page; the default shell registration uses the empty feed).
- useUnits / convertTempFromSI / convertDistanceFromSI / convertEnergyFromSI →
                                UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi/DistanceFromSi/EnergyFromSi +
                                ScalarFormatters at the display boundary (SI on the wire: °C, km*1000→metres,
                                Wh). UnitPref flows ViewModel → BatteryHealthProjection.Project(... units ...).
- i18n t(...)                 → ILocalizer.GetString(webKey, englishDefault) via BatteryHealthStrings.Resolve;
                                web key names preserved verbatim. The ShellLocalizer is resw-backed (the same
                                Strings/{lang}/Resources.resw pipeline the shell chrome uses) with the English
                                default as fallback in headless/unpackaged contexts — the established sibling
                                convention (BatteryDegradationPage resolves its keys the identical way).
- SectionErrorBoundary        → BatteryHealthPage.Section(fallbackTitle, build) guard — surfaces the localized
                                section-failed title if a section build throws (the 10 battery.section.* keys).

